 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"B2B Landing Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a B2B landing page?\", \"a\": \"A B2B landing page is a standalone page that asks another business for one action, usually a demo request, a quote, or a content download. It is written for a buying team instead of a single shopper. Expect proof from peer companies and a qualifying question or two, such as company size.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build B2B landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Pick one buyer and one action, such as a demo request, before you write anything. Then describe the page and the rule for who gets each lead to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It writes the sections and the form, and saves every submission to a lead table. Change any section with a follow-up prompt before you publish.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do great B2B landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"Great B2B landing pages speak to one role, such as a VP of finance, and put a customer quote from a company their size beside the form. Everything else on the page points at a single next step. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/webinar-landing-page'>webinar landing page</a> follows the same pattern, with a registration form where the demo request would sit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best practices for a B2B landing page?\", \"a\": \"The B2B landing page best practices that matter most start with one offer per page and a headline that matches the ad or email behind the click. Keep the form visible without scrolling on a laptop screen. When you test, change one element at a time; two edits at once hide which one moved the result.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you design B2B landing pages for lead generation?\", \"a\": \"Design B2B lead generation landing pages around an offer worth a work email, such as a benchmark report or a cost calculator. Ask for the email first and the company details on a second screen. On Emergent, each lead is saved to a database you own, and the form has no cap on responses.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a personalized B2B landing page?\", \"a\": \"It is a page made for one named account instead of a whole market, which is why marketers also call it an ABM personalized landing page. Sales sends the link straight to people at that company, and the copy speaks to their situation. With Emergent, a single prompt builds the template, and you can export its code to GitHub on paid plans.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields do the best B2B landing pages ask for?\", \"a\": \"A work email, plus one or two fields that sales acts on right away, usually company size or region. Phone number and job title are better asked on the call itself. Every extra field gives a busy buyer one more reason to close the tab.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track leads from B2B landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Record the campaign source with every lead, using the UTM tags on the link that brought the visitor in. Then compare pages by the meetings and deals each one produces. Sending the form to a thank you page gives your analytics a clean conversion event to count.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should you add navigation to a B2B landing page?\", \"a\": \"No. Leave the full site menu off a campaign page and keep the logo as the one link back to the main site. Buyers who want detail still need a route to it: a footer link to your <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/pricing-page'>pricing page</a> does that job.\"},{\"q\": \"What are the best B2B landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"The best B2B landing pages name the buyer's industry in the headline and show a result from a peer company near a short form. Example roundups and design galleries help with layout. On LinkedIn ABM landing pages, open with the same promise as the ad the account clicked.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
